+> broken-mirror-1@0.0.1 validate:ships
+> node bm-ships/validate.mjs
+
+PASS 174 distinct records; 172 active and two retired
+PASS All 152 BM2 source IDs resolve; Galaxy Dreadnaught maps to 49, not 60
+PASS Every asset is inside this pack, hash-verified and referenced
+PASS Every image crop and baseline draw size is valid
+PASS 26 redirects only new references to 211; retired 63 remains loadable
+PASS Excalibur, independent capital and Galaxy Dreadnaught are distinct
+PASS Five approved hulls have full balance; civilian shuttles start with empty armable slots
+PASS Blender gets scouts/fighters, not Dominion cruisers or battleships
+PASS Dominion core keeps its heavy ships; only authorized deployments leave
+PASS Gorn stays reserved; tactical cube requires an authored mission
+PASS No illegal fallback when a faction has no permitted local hulls
+PASS Faction standing travels with the captain; credits and another faction cannot substitute
+PASS Secret stock and regional sales require the corresponding vendor/context
+PASS Changing class scale preserves the aspect ratio and the per-hull envelope
+14/14 content/helper checks passed. No game-engine integration is implied.
+
+> broken-mirror-1@0.0.1 test:ships:economy
+> node scripts/ship-economy-probe.mjs
+
+PASS freeze acknowledges the final game loop
+PASS starting faction has 20 standing; another faction starts at 0
+PASS foreign concessions retain their own trade reputation
+PASS McKinley keeps Steamrunner rather than a Dominion ID collision
+PASS money alone cannot buy a capital for self, escort or garrison
+PASS one Terran standing unlocks the same design in two regions
+PASS changing a flag does not create or erase standing
+PASS Excalibur needs 100 Terran standing, not money or Ferengi trust
+PASS X-Base stocks distinct Galaxy Dreadnaught and Excalibur
+PASS real purchase installs Excalibur at the approved cost and stats
+PASS personal purchase gate also protects fleet paths
+PASS Concord uses independent trade standing
+PASS independent endgame vendor sells Concord, never Excalibur
+PASS real Basic Shuttle purchase costs 900 and selects its own hull
+PASS unarmed purchase preserves three empty slots even with weapons in inventory
+PASS authored empty NPC loadout cannot fire or manufacture aggression
+PASS firing an empty player slot creates no shot
+PASS unarmed shuttle can buy and equip a compatible weapon
+PASS the newly armed shuttle damages a target with the real weapon path
+PASS armed shuttle loadout and faction standing survive save/reload
+PASS intentionally empty loadout survives save/reload
+PASS delivery fixture is accepted with cargo
+PASS completed delivery earns destination trust and issuer trust
+PASS repeating delivery cannot claim the same standing twice
+PASS buy/sell cycling cannot buy its way to capital-ship trust
+PASS Blender purchases remain scout/fighter remnants
+PASS Dominica stocks cruiser 216 and battlecruiser 48, never Concord 60
+PASS core-region stock permits heavy Dominion purchases away from Blender
+PASS new Bird of Prey is between Brel and Kvort in durability and price
+PASS purchase UI shows required and current faction standing
+30/30 live economy checks passed
+
+> broken-mirror-1@0.0.1 test:ships:merges
+> node scripts/hull-merge-probe.mjs
+
+PASS all 38 approved references resolve to one canonical hull each
+PASS legacy-manifest entries cannot resurrect aliases or duplicate survivors
+PASS alias validation rejects cycles, missing targets and IDs that still have records
+PASS reviewed prices coexist with the approved artwork selections and Defiant anchor
+PASS source IDs, regional pools and explicit station stock contain no discarded hulls
+PASS five variant pairs and the requested unique BM2 hulls remain active
+PASS game loop freezes
+PASS starting hull resolves Ferengi #18 to #316
+PASS live roster and ship selector have exactly 172 active hulls
+PASS all old IDs are absent from runtime records but resolve to selected survivors
+PASS NPC construction uses canonical hull while preserving political identity
+PASS a yard listing both old and new IDs offers each hull once
+PASS old and canonical IDs share faction-standing gates in all three purchase paths
+PASS buying the old Defiant reference charges 62500 and stores hull #326
+PASS escort and garrison commissioning store canonical IDs
+PASS the current ship cannot be repurchased through its old alias
+PASS civilian and Imperial Ambassador fits are distinct and use three slots
+PASS upgraded Akira has a heavy beam and twin quantum fit
+PASS Steamrunner strike frigate has its own three-weapon fit
+PASS Imperial Ambassador and strike Akira have stronger NPC starting fire than their base variants
+PASS every explicit starting weapon fits its hull mass
+PASS civilian shuttles retain empty, armable three-slot layouts
+PASS Vulcan Explorer uses the approved native scale rounded to screen pixels
+23/23 hull merge checks passed
+
+> broken-mirror-1@0.0.1 test:ships:balance
+> node scripts/ship-balance-probe.mjs
+
+PASS all 172 active hulls have a role, rationale, explicit faction gate and reviewed capabilities
+PASS every supplied slot is explicit, defined and compatible with its hull; no obsolete ID fit leaks
+PASS same-class retained variants provide deliberate upgrades or civilian/military tradeoffs
+PASS early progression and specialist tradeoffs replace the old price inversions
+PASS all faction gates work just below and at their threshold without host tier configuration
+PASS supercapital gates and region restrictions survive the full balance pass
+PASS empty and utility-only craft cannot be selected as armed patrols or invasion ships
+PASS live game loop freezes
+PASS all 172 hulls instantiate and keep their exact three slots despite poisoned legacy item rows
+PASS all live hull, shield, cargo, impulse, fuel and range values match the authored capabilities
+PASS repricing every hull leaves its warp range unchanged
+PASS NPC primary weapons match supplied compatible combat equipment; empty and utility craft emit no aggression
+PASS every initially noncombat hull accepts a compatible weapon in a real equipment slot
+PASS fast scout and freighter differ in actual player speed, NPC speed and turning
+PASS Defiant is faster and more agile than Dderidex; the warbird carries far more protection and cargo
+PASS upgraded Akira adds real fitted damage potential and preserves both quantum launchers
+PASS survey and support fits are not hidden assault loadouts
+PASS purchase details show the role, all three supplied slots and shields
+PASS no cheaper same-faction same-market hull dominates every measured capability and included device
+19/19 full-roster balance checks passed
