+@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
++
++> broken-mirror-1@0.0.1 test:power:ingame
++> node scripts/ship-power-probe.mjs
++
++PASS main loop freezes for deterministic engine scenarios
++PASS every authored hull power profile reaches the actual engine
++PASS player and NPC on identical hull/fit/allocations pay the same weapon cost
++PASS player allocation cannot leak into an NPC flying the same hull
++PASS weapon allocation increases actual player damage and shot cost without changing recharge
++PASS NPC weapon allocation increases its own damage and shot cost
++PASS depleted NPC emits no shot, cooldown or aggression evidence
++PASS successful NPC shot debits exactly once and records attribution
++PASS depleted player emits no shot and does not spend cooldown
++PASS failed disruptive device activations do not spend cooldown or create player attack evidence
++PASS equal ships recover the same shield percentage for the same energy despite legacy durability units
++PASS legacy regeneration path does not refill ship shields a second time
++PASS two fitted secondary cores double output once, never capacity or stored energy
++PASS removing core removes output bonus immediately
++PASS insufficient continuous power disengages the real player cloak
++PASS real flight tick respects engine allocation and accelerates only with supplied propulsion
++PASS all four crew profiles fight through the real weapon path
++PASS veteran and elite crews preserve more reserve and spend less time near exhaustion than inexperienced crews
++PASS fleet creation restores energy and independently assigned skill/temperament
++PASS escort energy and crew survive system travel
++PASS cached foreign ship keeps energy and crew across return and change of holder
++PASS ambient replacement gets its own full initial power and valid crew, with a different seed
++PASS save/reload preserves player and fleet energy without stale live state overwriting the save
++PASS checkpoint snapshot sanitation preserves power and crew fields
++PASS OPS displays generation, demand, reserves and recovery/drain label
++PASS OPS has four functional sliders and a read-only unused-allocation count
++PASS raising a system spends spare points before reducing other systems
++PASS a full allocation budget redistributes without exceeding twenty points
++PASS all twenty points can be unused and the removed reserve control cannot change allocation
++{"encounters":{"inexperienced":{"min":0.010000000000008166,"shots":74,"low":1145,"recovered":false},"regular":{"min":0.1200916666666765,"shots":75,"low":0,"recovered":false},"veteran":{"min":0.2201583333333214,"shots":79,"low":0,"recovered":false},"elite":{"min":0.3000249999999866,"shots":81,"low":0,"recovered":false}}}
++29/29 live power checks passed
