+  PASS  S5.1 open access: a visitor crosses an enabled open zone; no order, objective, offence, hostility, standing change or shot
+  PASS  S5.17 tightening open access while a visitor is already inside issues a withdrawal in the same visit
+  PASS  S5.2 challenge: one order, the civilian approaches, holds through the dwell, is cleared with scope movement_identity and resumes its route; identity untouched
+  PASS  S5.3 closed: one withdrawal instruction; the civilian leaves, is recorded withdrawn (scope withdrawal), takes an outside lane, and gets no clearance
+  PASS  S5.4 refusal/expiry under return-fire: a calm war-flag visitor expires; noncompliance recorded once; no hostility, raid flag, aggro or standing change; escorts and turrets do not fire
+  PASS  S5.5 real aggression under the same policy still permits defence; stale evidence does not; no clearance is implied
+  PASS  S5.7 classification: own side exempt, same-flag foreigner other, unbranded hull independent, war flag, declared custom polity other, unidentified enforceable with default open
+  PASS  S5.10 time: the local clock follows the simulated delta, not wall or unloaded time; engine loss and combat end orders without fault; an order in an unloaded system keeps its remaining time and resumes on the same slot
+  PASS  S5.11 save/reload during approach and during dwell: same participant, order, remaining time, declared broadcast and dwell; no duplicate, refilled hull or repeated incident; the check then completes
+  PASS  S5.12 a replacement on the same slot is a new instance with no order or clearance; the old order closes; boundary jitter is not a new episode, a separated re-entry is
+  PASS  S5.13 capture ends orders as authority_changed and bumps the epoch; retained configuration and override command nothing under the occupier; reclaim restores the checkpoint but no old order
+  PASS  S5.14 operator UI: access click changes one dimension; waive (not verified), request withdrawal (revision), cancel; stricter access revises the same order, relaxation closes it without fault; reconfiguration closes without fault
+  PASS  S5.15 anchor destroyed: the order ends as checkpoint_unavailable without blame and the configuration is kept; a legacy save loads with no zones or orders; invalid records recover without crashing or orphan objectives
+  PASS  S5.8 player at the Vulcan checkpoint: placed outside on arrival, ordered on crossing, refused docking while pending, clearance request refused off-marker, repeat keeps the timer, cleared after holding, then docks; aggression revokes clearance; foreign policy not editable
+  PASS  S5.9 player withdraw resolves only on physical exit and grants no clearance; refusal closes the order, is recorded, blocks docking, creates no hostility or standing change; a completed jump ends the visit
+  PASS  S5.16 isolation: a hostile ship is never addressed and stays a target; a waiver changes no fleet orders or hostility
+  PASS  S3i enemy defenders select and engage a player escort attacking their installation
